WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.734
-Our first guest tonight
is an Emmy-nominated actor,

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.367
comedian, you know from
"30 Rock"

00:00:04.367 --> 00:00:06.067
and his work
on "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:08.601
New episodes of his show,
"The Last O.G."

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.267
air Tuesday nights on TBS.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:11.767
Please welcome back to the show

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.801
our very good friend
Tracy Morgan.

00:00:13.801 --> 00:00:15.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.801 --> 00:00:25.801
♪♪

00:00:25.801 --> 00:00:33.534
♪♪

00:00:33.534 --> 00:00:35.834
-Tracy Morgan!

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:38.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.234 --> 00:00:39.601
-What up, what up,
what up, Seth?

00:00:39.601 --> 00:00:40.901
Roy, Roy!
Roy, Roy!

00:00:40.901 --> 00:00:42.701
[ Laughter ]
What up, Roy?

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.901
-Yo! What's up?
-Can I get my $10 back?

00:00:44.901 --> 00:00:46.200
[ Laughter ]
-[ Grunts ]

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.734
-You owe me $10.
-Now, last I saw you,

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.734
we Zoomed two weeks
into the pandemic,

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:53.400
and I got to tell you, Tracy,
I think it was the first time

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.200
I laughed
after the pandemic started.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.567
You were so funny,
and it's so good to see you.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:59.601
How are you feeling these days?
-I'm feeling great.

00:00:59.601 --> 00:01:01.767
I'm just a little distressed.
'Cause my name --

00:01:01.767 --> 00:01:03.801
My name keeps coming up
and everything, man.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:05.367
-How so?
-They stormed the Capitol,

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.367
my name came up.
-How so?

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.501
-Michelle Obama get pregnant,
my name come up.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:10.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:12.400
Two girls and a cup,
my name come up.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:13.868
-Really?
-Yeah!

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.467
-That's good!
You're in the zeitgeist.

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:17.100
-Man, my name keep coming up
in everything.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.300
-Yeah.
I want to talk about

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.033
show business with you,
as I always do,

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:22.734
but I also want to talk about

00:01:22.734 --> 00:01:25.200
some things that I also know
are important to you.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.234
Inflation --
Inflation and the economy.

00:01:28.234 --> 00:01:29.968
[ Laughter ]
-I'm gonna keep my eye on them.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.834
-Yeah, keep your eye on them.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:33.801
-Do you have any --
-Inflation is crazy.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:34.968
-Yeah, what about --

00:01:34.968 --> 00:01:36.767
-Prices are going up
through the roof, man.

00:01:36.767 --> 00:01:40.234
I just got some sound, good
advice for my financial adviser.

00:01:40.234 --> 00:01:42.133
He said, "You should wait
at least a year

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.968
before you get hit
by another Walmart truck."

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:45.567
-Got it.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.567 --> 00:01:47.767
-At least one year.

00:01:47.767 --> 00:01:49.567
And I listened to him.
I gotta listen.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.267
I'm going for Amazon now,
though.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.167
-Oh, interesting.
That's good idea.

00:01:53.167 --> 00:01:55.033
-I'm going big now, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.467
-What about labor shortages?
Have you seen this in your life?

00:01:57.467 --> 00:01:59.400
-Yeah, labor shortages.
They out there, man.

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:00.701
I went to the strip club,

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:02.067
there was only one stripper
in the whole club.

00:02:02.067 --> 00:02:03.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:05.667
She gave me, like,
one lap dance on 16.

00:02:05.667 --> 00:02:07.534
The same mixtape.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:08.801
She stopped
taking her clothes off.

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.100
She said,
"You already saw my booty."

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:11.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.834
"You don't need
to see it again."

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:15.467
-Very frustrating.
Did you get vaccinated?

00:02:15.467 --> 00:02:18.167
Are you happy to be vaccinated?
-Yeah, I got vaccinated.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:20.234
But it wasn't for COVID,
it was for gonorrhea.

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:23.834
-Oh, okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:27.434
-Keeping my mind
where it should be.

00:02:27.434 --> 00:02:28.634
-I hope -- This is --

00:02:28.634 --> 00:02:30.367
You know, we kind of
referenced it earlier.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:32.334
This is a good time to be
a New York Knicks fan, Tracy.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:33.367
Are you enjoying it?
-Yeah, man.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:35.567
This, right here,
is a lucky log.

00:02:35.567 --> 00:02:37.234
All the Knick fans --
I'm representing --

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:39.467
I'm representing the culture.
So all the Knicks --

00:02:39.467 --> 00:02:40.734
all the Knicks, the players,

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:42.167
they come and rub this
for a win.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:44.100
-When you go to the games,
they come over and they rub it.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:46.534
-When I go to the game.
They doing good, too.

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:47.734
-Yeah.
-They look like

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:49.400
they like playing together.
I like it.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.133
-And you bring your daughter
to the games?

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:53.834
-I be -- Oh, boo,
that's my Stinky Mama.

00:02:53.834 --> 00:02:56.067
-Yeah.
-I call her Stinky Mama.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:57.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.367 --> 00:02:59.334
You know, most fathers,
they gotta whistle,

00:02:59.334 --> 00:03:00.934
and they kids come.
[ Imitates whistling ]

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:02.801
And the kids come.
But with her,

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.834
all I gotta do is go,
"Aaaaaaah!"

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:06.334
and she come running.
-Wow.

00:03:06.334 --> 00:03:07.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:10.234
-"Aaaaaaaah!"
-Can you whistle, though, Tracy?

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:11.300
'Cause when you just said --
-Can I whistle?

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.100
-Yeah.
You said a lot of --

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:16.534
-Do I look like a magician?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:17.767
I don't be whistling.

00:03:17.767 --> 00:03:20.100
Whistling for what?
"Aaaaaaah da-laaah!"

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.234
-That's way better.
-Come on.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.701
So if we go to Disney World,
and, like,

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.133
she get lost
in all those people,

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:27.000
all I got to do is go, "Aaaah!"
and she come running.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.801
-That's great.
And that must be nice

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:31.000
for the other families, as well.
-That's my Stinky Mama, yeah.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.267
All the other families.

00:03:32.267 --> 00:03:34.767
-What was your -- Halloween?
Did Megan dress up?

00:03:34.767 --> 00:03:36.868
-Halloween is getting crazy
out there.

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:38.000
It's just different
than when I grew up.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:39.801
I mean, these white kids
in my neighborhood,

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:42.133
'cause I live in the suburbs
now, since Walmart.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:43.968
I live in the suburbs.
-Right.

00:03:43.968 --> 00:03:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.701 --> 00:03:51.934
So I live in the suburbs.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.601
I'm watching this dude
over here.

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.467
[ Laughter ]
I live in the suburbs.

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:57.334
The white kids,
they like rap now.

00:03:57.334 --> 00:03:58.634
They dressing the part.

00:03:58.634 --> 00:04:00.234
They listening to rap
and all that.

00:04:00.234 --> 00:04:01.567
But one of them
little white kids came up

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:02.601
and was trick-or-treating.

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:04.400
Yes, came to my house,
was a ghost.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:05.801
So, I said,
"Who you supposed to be?"

00:04:05.801 --> 00:04:07.334
He said, "I'm a ghost."
I said "Why the --"

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:09.400
The sheet was black.
-He was wearing a black sheet?

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.267
-A black sheet.
I said "Why the [bleep] --"

00:04:11.267 --> 00:04:12.300
Excuse me.
-That's all right.

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:13.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.534
-I said, "Well,
why your sheet is black?"

00:04:15.534 --> 00:04:17.167
He said,
"'Cause I'm keeping it real."

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:20.601
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:21.834
-What about you?
When you grew up,

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:24.067
what were your Halloweens like?
-My Halloween?

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:27.467
I didn't get dressed up
until I was 38.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:28.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:29.868
-What was it like
in your neighborhood?

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:32.133
-I dressed up as a cop.
I got whatever I wanted.

00:04:32.133 --> 00:04:35.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.167 --> 00:04:39.701
I was a bag man.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:42.467
I was a bad cop.
I dressed up as a bad cop.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.300
-All right.
-I was a -- I dressed up --

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.801
What was his name?

00:04:45.801 --> 00:04:47.234
What was the cop,
the good cop name?

00:04:47.234 --> 00:04:49.300
What was his name?
-Serpico.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:51.534
-Yeah.
I was a bad cop after him.

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:52.934
-Oh, really?
-Yeah, I was --

00:04:52.934 --> 00:04:54.934
-So you were not --
you were not Frank Serpico.

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:58.601
-I was on "the take."
-So, you dressed up -- your --

00:04:58.601 --> 00:05:00.834
-I would go
to illegal gambling spots

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:02.434
and got --
get whatever I wanted.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:04.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:07.267
At illegal gambling spots.

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:09.467
-Do you feel like we have
enough illegal gambling spots

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:11.200
in the city anymore?
-There's not enough.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.701
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:15.234
-I'm not getting paid.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:15.234 --> 00:05:17.667
-How would you get paid?
-I would go on "the take."

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:19.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:22.334
I'd take bribes and everything.
I'm a bad cop.

00:05:22.334 --> 00:05:23.601
[ Laughter ]
-I want --

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:26.334
-All I got to do
is pull out a phone book.

00:05:26.334 --> 00:05:27.501
-Oh, is that --

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:28.801
-Hit them in the head
with the phone book.

00:05:28.801 --> 00:05:30.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:32.567
Get whatever you want.
-That was part of your costume?

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:34.701
You carry around a phone book?
-I need information.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.667
-Yeah.
So would you say --

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:38.634
when you showed up dressed like
a bad cop with a phone book,

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:39.801
would you even say,
"Trick or treat,"

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:42.734
or would you just say, uh --
-"Give it up."

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:44.934
[ Laughter ]

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.133
I don't believe
in, "Trick or treat."

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:47.968
"Give it up."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:49.634
I'm getting ready
to get a tattoo on my hand.

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.067
-What's it gonna say?
-"Pay me."

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:52.868
-Really?
That's pretty nice.

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:54.334
-"Pay me."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:54.334 --> 00:05:56.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:57.601
I've got some more questions
for you.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:06:00.067
You gonna stick around?
-I'm around. I'm here.

00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:02.467
-We'll be right back with more
from Tracy Morgan.

